<title>USA: Clark Blue Island, Illinois refinery to stay open.</title>
<headline>Clark Blue Island, Illinois refinery to stay open.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>- A judge ruled Friday that Clark Refining &amp; Marketing can keep its Blue Island, Illinois refinery open.</p>
<p>Cook County circuit court judge Albert Green said the plant had undergone &quot;rigorous inspection,&quot; allowing the reopening of two units closed weeks ago by a fire.</p>
<p>An October 19 fire and explosion shut the plant's propane &quot;scrubber&quot; and an alcylation unit, and resulted in a late October hearing on the safety of the refinery.</p>
<p>Judge Green said the fire at the units was not a &quot;substantial threat to human life,&quot; and subsequent inspections allayed safety concerns.</p>
<p>Blue Island has an operating capacity of around 80,000 barrels per day (bpd), but was running at only 55,000 bpd since the two units were shut.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
